---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import QuoteBanner from '../components/shared/QuoteBanner.astro';
import PhotoCarousel from '../components/shared/PhotoCarousel.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="What is Montessori for Adolescents?"
  description="Montessori for adolescents is education built for the third plane of development, roughly ages twelve to eighteen: meaningful work, real responsibility, and an environment prepared around the adolescent."
  heroTitle="What is Montessori for Adolescents?"
  heroImage="/images/whole-human-hero.jpg"
>
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <section class="page-section">
      <p>
        Montessori for adolescents is education designed for students aged 12
        to 18. The adolescent is drawn to do work that genuinely matters, to
        belong to a community of peers, and to begin to understand their place
        in the wider world.
      </p>
      <p>
        Maria Montessori called her vision for this age <em>Erdkinder</em>, the
        children of the land: a school where young people take real
        responsibility for a farm, a kitchen, a shop, and discover what they
        are capable of by doing it. The setting varies enormously from school
        to school, but the principles travel: meaningful work, real
        responsibility, and an environment prepared around the adolescent
        rather than around a subject timetable. The adolescent draws a little
        distance from the family during these years, so that they can develop
        their authentic self and their own abilities.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section">
      <h2>How Montessori differs from traditional education</h2>
      <p>
        Imagine a community where each young person is given room to breathe,
        unfold, and grow into their most authentic self.
      </p>
      <p>
        Montessori education gives the adolescent room for self-expression:
        working alongside adults from many different professions, and trying
        their hand at art, music and language.
      </p>
      <p>
        School is not dictated by classes and bells. The days are given to work
        and study together, and students manage their own time, balancing
        duties on the farm, an hour with the mathematics instructor, and lunch
        to cook for the community.
      </p>
      <p>
        The adolescent environment gives students a real chance to work, to
        bond, and to take care of one another. What they do has consequences
        for how the whole community runs. They are depended upon, and they
        depend on others.
      </p>
      <p>
        Montessori pedagogy rests on a profound understanding of adolescent
        development, and it nurtures the whole person, always keeping the
        interconnected nature of life in view.
      </p>
      <p>
        The result is young people who believe in themselves and in what they
        can do, and who have lived that interconnection rather than been told
        about it. They tend to be innately curious, to care for all beings, and
        to be guided by intrinsic motivation. Montessori is an education for a
        more peaceful world.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="carousel-section">
    <PhotoCarousel photos={[
      { src: '/images/whole-human-photo-1.jpg', alt: 'Adolescents at work in a Montessori environment' },
      { src: '/images/whole-human-photo-2.jpg', alt: 'Adolescents at work in a Montessori environment' },
      { src: '/images/whole-human-photo-3.jpg', alt: 'Adolescents at work in a Montessori environment' },
      { src: '/images/whole-human-photo-4.jpg', alt: 'Adolescents at work in a Montessori environment' },
    ]} />
  </div>

  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <section class="page-section">
      <h2>What adolescents need</h2>
      <div class="dimensions">
        <div class="dimension">
          <h3>Intellectual</h3>
          <p>Critical thinking, curiosity, and the capacity for abstract reasoning that emerges in the third plane.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dimension">
          <h3>Emotional</h3>
          <p>Self-awareness, resilience, and the ability to navigate the intense emotional landscape of adolescence.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dimension">
          <h3>Social</h3>
          <p>Belonging, collaboration, and understanding one's role within the community and the wider world.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dimension">
          <h3>Physical</h3>
          <p>Connection to the body, meaningful physical work, and practices that honor the adolescent's changing form.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dimension">
          <h3>Moral</h3>
          <p>A developing sense of justice, responsibility, and the courage to act on one's values.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

  <QuoteBanner
    text="The greatest sign of success for a teacher is to be able to say, 'The children are now working as if I did not exist.'"
    author="Maria Montessori"
  />
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .page-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .page-section h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    color: var(--color-earth);
  }

  .page-section p {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .dimensions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .dimension {
    background-color: var(--color-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-xl);
    flex: 0 1 calc(33.333% - var(--space-lg));
    min-width: 220px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .dimension {
      flex: 0 1 100%;
    }
  }

  .dimension h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    color: var(--color-terracotta);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .dimension p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .carousel-section {
    margin-block: var(--space-3xl);
  }
</style>
